  "problem": "Consider the following statement.\n\n$5$ does **not** divide $20.$\n\nWhat is the negation of this statement?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's denote the given statement as $P.$\n\nThe symbol \"$\u00ac$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\nIt is **not** true that $5$  does **not** divide $20.$\n\nIn other words, $5$ divides $20.$ Therefore, $\u00acP$ means the following:\n\n$5$ divides $20.$\n\nNote that $P$ is **false,** while $\u00acP$ is **true.**",
